    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1127">

                <pb facs="1387" n="1373" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg1373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 E W /2–1945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-19T19:00:00-04:00">February 19,
                            1945—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>80. Reurtel 131, February 19, 10 a.m.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d1127-f1"/> For
                    Uruguay to be invited to the San Francisco Conference it should act by March 1.
                    This is in accordance with a decision taken at Yalta.<anchor n="25"
                        xml:id="d1127-f2"/> Please inform President confidentially.</p>
                <p>After the declaration of war and before a representative of Uruguay signs the
                    United Nations Declaration, we should have a communication stating that Uruguay
                    has entered into a state of war, that it desires to adhere to the United Nations
                    Declaration, and that it has empowered a representative to sign on behalf of
                    Uruguay.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
